[center][size=5][b]Bigger Item Grids and Smaller Inventory Slots[/b][/size]
Inventory increases from 5 rows to [b]7 rows[/b] visible, technology from 3 to [b]4 rows[/b], and the
Transfer/Craft popups from 8 slots to [b]24 slots[/b] per page[/center]
[b]What it does[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Inventory: [/b]Increase visible rows from 5 to [b]7[/b], Technology from 3 to [b]4[/b].[/*]
[*][b]Transfer Items and Craft Product popups: [/b]Increase from 4 by 2 (8 slots per page) to [b]8 by 3 (24 slots per page)[/b][/*]
[/list]

[b]Requires:[/b] the [b]Nozavolochen Framework[/b] file (provides the host DLL).

[b]Toggles:[/b]

Edit the included [b]mod.toml[/b] in the mod folder under [b]GAMEDATA/MODS[/b]. `popup_pages` and `inventory_grid` must both be `true` for the bigger inventory to function.
Press backtick (`) in game to open the settings panel and change the toggles live instead.

Part of the [b]Nozavolochen[/b] mod family (one shared host DLL, spec-driven mods - no closed-source loaders). Intro skip and mod-warning skip are separate mods.

[b]Install[/b]

Import the zip as a normal mod (Amethyst/Vortex) or drop its contents
into the game folder.



[b]Compatibility[/b]
[list]
[*]Modifies the popup, inventory page, slot and box UI files, plus
pattern-scanned hooks for the grid and page size.
Nothing else[/*]
[*]Built for Forsaken - a game update can shift the patterns, and the log
will say so instead of misbehaving[/*]
[*][b].lua [/b]included so you can merge with AMUMSS[/*]
[/list]
Built natively on Linux with my [url=https://github.com/SavageCore/AMUMSS/tree/feat/linux-support]AMUMSS Linux port[/url].

Source: [url=https://github.com/SavageCore/bigger-item-grids-and-smaller-inventory-slots]https://github.com/SavageCore/bigger-item-grids-and-smaller-inventory-slots[/url]